using System;

// Independently written summaries, linked to their guides; no build is applied automatically.
public sealed class CuratedBuild {
 public readonly string Name,Details;
 public CuratedBuild(string name,string details){Name=name;Details=details;}
 public override string ToString(){return Name;}
}
public static class CuratedBuilds {
 public static readonly CuratedBuild[] Warlock={
  new CuratedBuild("Demon Summoner", "WARLOCK  /  DEMON SUMMONER\r\n\r\nA practical, mostly self-found path from your first Goatman through Hell. Your demons do the fighting while you direct them, keep them alive, and build your own defenses. This guide is advice: it does not change your saved build.\r\n\r\nFIRST GOALS\r\n1. Summon Goatman, then build Demonic Mastery toward 5 invested points for a second demon and 10 for a third.\r\n2. Make Stealth armor and keep a weapon or grimoire with useful Warlock or Demon skills.\r\n3. Add Lore, a Spirit sword, and an Insight polearm for an Act II mercenary as the runes and suitable bases become available.\r\n4. Before advancing difficulties, replace weak pieces with life and resistances. +skills are powerful, but staying alive comes first.\r\n\r\nSKILL PRIORITIES / PROGRESSION\r\nEarly levels: Put a point in Summon Goatman, then invest in Demonic Mastery as your level allows. At 5 hard points you can have two demons; at 10 hard points you can have three. Hard points are the points you spend yourself. Bonuses from gear improve the skill but do not unlock these demon-count thresholds.\r\n\r\nAt level 6: Take Death Mark to focus your demons on a dangerous target. Blood Oath is a useful defensive option; keep an eye on your demon's health when using it.\r\n\r\nAt levels 12-24: Try Summon Tainted for a ranged option and Summon Defiler for another demon choice. Add the prerequisites for Blood Boil and Engorge as they become available. Engorge uses a corpse to help an injured demon; Blood Boil gives you a way to add damage around a demon.\r\n\r\nAt level 30 and later: Unlock Bind Demon through its prerequisites and try binding an eligible enemy demon. Elite binding depends on hard points in Bind Demon: 10 for champions, 15 for uniques, and 20 for super uniques. Gear bonuses do not satisfy these requirements. Some bosses or monsters cannot be bound; check the skill in game.\r\n\r\nLONG-TERM POINTS\r\nFor a pure summoner, work toward 20 hard points each in Demonic Mastery, Summon Goatman, Bind Demon, and Blood Oath. Spend a point on prerequisites and useful supporting skills first, then finish the larger investments as you level. You can favor other demons or Blood Boil if you enjoy them more. This is a direction, not a strict point-by-point order; the planner shows available points and prerequisites.\r\n\r\nATTRIBUTES\r\nStrength: Enough to wear the equipment you actually plan to use. Dexterity: Only what your chosen equipment requires unless you deliberately build for blocking. Vitality: Put most remaining points here for life. Energy: Usually leave it alone and solve mana problems with potions, equipment, or an Insight mercenary. Save attribute points if you are unsure of an upgrade's requirements.\r\n\r\nEARLY RUNEWORDS  /  MAKE IN THIS ORDER AS DROPS ALLOW\r\nStealth: Tal + Eth in a nonmagical 2-socket body armor. Usable from level 17 or the base's requirement, whichever is higher. Faster run/walk, cast rate and hit recovery make the whole journey smoother. It does not directly increase your demons' damage.\r\n\r\nAncient's Pledge: Ral + Ort + Tal in a nonmagical 3-socket shield. A useful resistance shield while leveling. The Act V rescue quest gives the three runes; insert them in the order shown here. Compare it with any Warlock grimoire you find: a shield and a grimoire are different base types.\r\n\r\nLore: Ort + Sol in a nonmagical 2-socket helm. +1 to all skills and lightning resistance make this a simple summoner upgrade. Sol makes the minimum level 27; a higher-level base can raise it. Nightmare Countess is a practical source of Sol, though drops are random.\r\n\r\nSpirit: Tal + Thul + Ort + Amn in a nonmagical 4-socket sword. +2 all skills, mana, hit recovery and faster casting make this a strong upgrade. The Amn rune requires level 25, but the base can require more. Find a suitable four-socket sword; do not assume every Crystal Sword will get four sockets from Larzuk. A Spirit shield is a separate option with different base restrictions: the commonly used Monarch needs 156 Strength. A Warlock grimoire is not a shield base.\r\n\r\nInsight: Ral + Tir + Tal + Sol in a nonmagical 4-socket polearm for an Act II mercenary. Its Meditation aura helps with mana regeneration while your mercenary is alive and nearby. The Sol rune requires level 27; check the polearm's requirements too. Spears are not polearms for this recipe. Insight also has other valid bases, but those are not the polearm recommendation for an Act II mercenary.\r\n\r\nRhyme: Shael + Eth in a nonmagical 2-socket shield. Cannot Be Frozen, resistances and magic find make it an alternative to Ancient's Pledge when you find Shael. It competes with a grimoire, so choose the defenses or skill bonuses you need most.\r\n\r\nRUNEWORD CHECKLIST\r\nUse the exact number of sockets and the exact rune order shown. The base must be a compatible nonmagical item; blue, yellow, set and unique items will not work. Ethereal items work, but ethereal player gear loses durability; an ethereal mercenary polearm can be a useful find. Check the Runewords tab for full effects and mode restrictions before spending runes. The equipment builder tracks supported bonuses, not every item effect.\r\n\r\nFARMING AND DIFFICULTY CHECKPOINTS\r\nNormal: Farm the Countess in the Forgotten Tower for common early runes and look for a 2-socket armor for Stealth. Shop and identify useful Warlock skill weapons and grimoires. Do the Act V rescue for Ancient's Pledge runes.\r\n\r\nNightmare: Revisit the Countess for mid-low runes, including a chance at Sol. Look for a 2-socket helm, a suitable 4-socket sword and a polearm for your mercenary. Loot is random; do not delay your whole playthrough waiting for a perfect base.\r\n\r\nHell: Resistances drop when changing difficulty, so check your character screen and improve weak resists before dangerous encounters. Farm places you can clear safely, and keep a backup plan for physical-immune monsters: try different demon damage types, your mercenary, party assistance, or skip the encounter. Move on when the risk or time cost is too high.\r\n\r\nOTHER EQUIPMENT\r\nWeapon and offhand: Compare +all skills, +Warlock skills, +Demon skills and bonuses to skills you use. A useful grimoire can be better for you than a shield, but you may need the shield's defenses.\r\nGloves, belt, boots, rings and amulet: Fill gaps in life, resistances, mana and movement speed. Faster cast rate helps your own casting, not your demons' attack speed. The Equipment breakpoint view can help compare your cast rate.\r\nCharms: Keep useful life and resistance charms; upgrade to skill charms when you find them and can afford the space. Leave enough inventory room for loot.\r\nMercenary: Keep their resistances and survivability in mind as well as their weapon. A dead mercenary provides no active aura; revive them when it is safe and affordable.\r\n\r\nPLAYING THE BUILD\r\nLet your demons enter first and use Death Mark on priority targets. Reposition when surrounded, use corpses for Engorge when appropriate, and resummon fallen demons. Keep potions handy for bosses and watch your own health even with Blood Oath. Try Goatman, Tainted, Defiler and a bound demon to find the mix you enjoy; the demon cap is shared.\r\n\r\nREFERENCES\r\nBlizzard's live Patch 3.2 notes explain the invested-point thresholds: https://news.blizzard.com/en-gb/article/24261478/diablo-ii-resurrected-ladder-season-14-has-concluded\r\nFurther build and equipment ideas: https://www.icy-veins.com/d2/demon-warlock-build\r\nRuneword details: use the in-app Runewords library. Game patches, ladder rules and available expansions can change; check your current game mode."),
  new CuratedBuild("Fire Caster", "WARLOCK  /  FIRE CASTER\r\n\r\nPLAYSTYLE\r\nAn area-damage caster using Ring of Fire, Flame Wave and Apocalypse. Particularly comfortable through early leveling, with fire immunity to consider later.\r\n\r\nSKILL PRIORITIES\r\nWork toward 20 points each in Ring of Fire, Flame Wave and Apocalypse; their invested points improve each other. Add prerequisites and consider Summon Tainted and Consume for a demon-assisted option.\r\n\r\nPROGRESSION\r\nStart with Ring of Fire, add Flame Wave when available and Apocalypse at level 30. Spend points as level requirements allow. Consider alternative damage, a mercenary or party help for fire-immune monsters.\r\n\r\nGEAR\r\nLook for +Fire or +Warlock skills, mana, cast rate and resistances. Leaf in a suitable staff is an early option; Spirit and stronger skill items are later upgrades.\r\n\r\nREFERENCE\r\nInspired by MrLlamaSC's Fire Warlock guide: https://www.icy-veins.com/d2/fire-warlock-build\r\n\r\nThis is guidance, not an automatic skill allocation. Check ladder and expansion availability for specific items."),
  new CuratedBuild("Magic Caster", "WARLOCK  /  MAGIC CASTER\r\n\r\nPLAYSTYLE\r\nUse Miasma skills and Abyss to control groups and deal magic damage over time. Position enemies within the clouds and use summons for support.\r\n\r\nSKILL PRIORITIES\r\nWork toward 20 points each in Miasma Bolt, Miasma Chain and Abyss. Invest in Enhanced Entropy, accounting for equipment skill levels, and consider Summon Defiler and Consume for support. Add prerequisites.\r\n\r\nPROGRESSION\r\nBegin with Miasma Bolt and add Miasma Chain and Abyss when available. This is a long-term goal, not a level-by-level allocation; unlock required skills first.\r\n\r\nGEAR\r\nPrioritize +Warlock or +Eldritch skills, cast rate, mana, life and resistances. Stealth, Lore and Spirit are useful equipment goals where available.\r\n\r\nREFERENCE\r\nInspired by MrLlamaSC's Magic Warlock guide: https://www.icy-veins.com/d2/magic-warlock-build\r\n\r\nThis is guidance, not an automatic skill allocation. Check ladder and expansion availability for specific items.")
 };
